.TH TULPAR-VERIFY 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.6.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-verify \- verify installed package files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar verify
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar v
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar \-v
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks that every file recorded for each installed package is still
present on disk, and reports any package with missing files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Verify an alternate root instead of the live system.
.TP
.B \-\-db
Also check the package database against itself. Reports package
records that cannot be read or are stored under another name, file
lists of packages that are not installed, listed files that have no
recorded owner or are owned by another package, and recorded owners
that are not installed or do not list the file. The files on disk are
not consulted for this check.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every installed package verified cleanly, non-zero if any file
is missing or, with
.BR \-\-db ,
the database is inconsistent.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-list (1)
